(B) the maximum
========================================================================================================
  max_(2<=q<=5000) M_odd(q) = 0.7071067812 at q = 4;  1/sqrt2 = 0.7071067812
  runner-up: (0.6299605249474366, 3)   (q=8, 2^(1/4-1) = 0.5946035575)
  best odd q: q=3, 2^(1/3-1) = 0.6299605249
  paper 2's reduced-residue maximum for comparison: sqrt3/2 = 0.8660254038 at q=6 (M_odd(6) = 0.0)
  So the two classes have DIFFERENT extremal moduli and different constants:
    reduced residues (the primes)  -> q = 6, sqrt3/2 = 0.8660
    odd residues (a random odd A)  -> q = 4, 1/sqrt2 = 0.7071

